<title>UK: Ranger Oil signs oil production deal.</title>
<headline>Ranger Oil signs oil production deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ranger Oil Ltd said on Wednesday it had signed a production sharing agreement with the government of the Cote d'Ivoire relating to offshore block CI-102.</p>
<p>The block lies immediately south of the capital Abidjan in water depths generally shallower than 200 metres. It lies between the Espoir oil field to the west and Belier oil field to the east.</p>
<p>Ranger Oil is operator for a group made up of Clyde Expro, a subsidiary of Gulf Canada Resources Ltd with 24 percent, Energy Africa Ltd (24 pct), Gentry Resources Ltd (11 pct), TC Petroleum Inc (5 pct) and Petroci (12 pct).</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
